<blockquote class="inline_help">
streamable-http: MCP server runs as an HTTP daemon on the configured port (recommended).
stdio: client-spawned transport for SSH-based clients (advanced).
</blockquote>

_(Enable stdio Transport)_:
: <select name="UNRAID_MCP_ENABLE_STDIO">
  <option value="false" <?=(!$stdioEnable) ? 'selected' : ''?>>No (default)</option>
  <option value="true" <?=($stdioEnable) ? 'selected' : ''?>>Yes</option>
  </select>
<blockquote class="inline_help">
Master gate for stdio. When No, the binary refuses to serve stdio entirely —
even if launched manually or via SSH. Enable only while you need it.
</blockquote>

<?php if (!$stdioMode): ?>
_(Bind Host)_:
: <input type="text" name="UNRAID_MCP_HOST" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($cfg('UNRAID_MCP_HOST', '0.0.0.0'))?>">
<blockquote class="inline_help">
Bind address for the MCP HTTP server. 0.0.0.0 allows remote clients (e.g. VS Code on another machine);
127.0.0.1 restricts to localhost. Use a bearer token for remote access.
</blockquote>

_(Port)_:
: <input type="number" name="UNRAID_MCP_PORT" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($mcpPort)?>" min="1024" max="65535">
<blockquote class="inline_help">
TCP port the MCP HTTP server listens on. This is the bind port — the port
the server listens on locally. If you expose it through a reverse proxy on
a different port, set that in <b>MCP Endpoint URL</b> below.
</blockquote>

_(MCP Endpoint URL)_:
: <input type="text" name="UNRAID_MCP_ENDPOINT" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($cfg('UNRAID_MCP_ENDPOINT'))?>">
<blockquote class="inline_help">
Full URL your MCP client (IDE/LM Studio) should use to reach the MCP server.
When set, this URL is used directly in the auto-generated client config below.
The path in this URL must be forwarded by your reverse proxy to the MCP server.
Leave blank to auto-derive from the Unraid API URL host + browser port.
</blockquote>
<blockquote class="inline_help">
<b>Reverse proxy setup:</b> your proxy must forward the path from your MCP Endpoint URL
to your Unraid server on port <b><?=$mcpPort?></b>. The MCP server handles any path
via its catch-all handler, so the path in your endpoint URL can be anything —
just make sure your proxy forwards it. Example nginx config for path
<code>/ua-mcp</code>:
<pre style="background:#0d1117;border-radius:4px;padding:8px;font-size:11px;">location /ua-mcp {
    proxy_pass http://unraid-local-ip:<?=$mcpPort?>;
    proxy_set_header Host $host;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    proxy_http_version 1.1;
    proxy_set_header Connection "";
    proxy_buffering off;
}</pre>
If your endpoint URL uses a non-standard path (e.g. <code>/ua-mcp</code>),
make sure your proxy forwards that <i>exact path</i> — not just <code>/mcp</code>.
</blockquote>
<?php else: ?>
<input type="hidden" name="UNRAID_MCP_HOST" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($cfg('UNRAID_MCP_HOST', '0.0.0.0'))?>">
<input type="hidden" name="UNRAID_MCP_PORT" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($mcpPort)?>">
